From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:22:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost/kbase: keep the driver's own never-exported dma-buf
 BOs CPU-coherent

With a dma-heap available, kbase_kmod_bo_alloc() backs every BO without an
exclusive VM with a dma-heap buffer that it imports through
kbase_kmod_import_dmabuf(). Besides exportable memory, that covers
host-visible memory when memoryMapPlaced is enabled, which Wine's Vulkan
layer does for 32-bit (WoW64) processes; DXVK's staging buffers in 32-bit
games land there. "import dma-bufs inner-shareable"
made all of these imports COHERENT_LOCAL, so the GPU stopped snooping the
CPU's cached dma-buf mapping: CPU writes still in the cache reach GPU copies
as zeros. In Batman: Arkham Asylum, whose DXT textures GameNative transcodes
to ASTC 8x8 on the CPU, the zero blocks decode to the ASTC error colour and
show as magenta specks on characters and loading-screen glyphs.

Add PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT, which PanVK sets on BOs that are shareable
only for placed maps, and import those COHERENT_SYSTEM again. Nobody else
maps them, so the shareability conflict the inner-shareable import avoids
can't happen; external imports and exportable memory stay COHERENT_LOCAL.
PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL=1 keeps the old behaviour.

Arkham Asylum, launch + checkpoint restart, interleaved, same build:
specks in 0/9 valid runs (fix) vs 6/7 (PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL=1), 10
rounds each; with a CPU wait after each submit, uploaded ASTC mips with
missing blocks 0 of 11006 vs 310 of 11005 in one launch. No GPU faults;
PanProbe 38/38 x3. Frame rate at 1255 MHz unchanged: Arkham 25.35 vs
25.15 fps; 64-bit Hades (no placed maps, untouched) 227.7 vs 228.5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: fix magenta specks / zero blocks in uploaded textures (Arkham Asylum) caused by rg477m/001: the driver's own never-exported dma-heap BOs (placed-map host memory, DXVK staging in 32-bit/WoW64 games) were imported inner-shareable, so the GPU did not snoop the CPU's cached writes; import those COHERENT_SYSTEM again (PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL=1 reverts)
Upstream-commit: none (kbase backend only)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/001 (fixes it); applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/020
Validation test: Arkham Asylum launch + checkpoint restart, interleaved on one build: specks 0/9 valid runs vs 6/7 with PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL=1 (10 rounds per arm, one-sided Fisher p<0.001); ASTC mips with missing blocks after copy 0 of 11006 vs 310 of 11005 in one launch; game context imports 2278 outer (c43e) + 19 exported inner (c23e); no GPU faults in 20 runs; PanProbe 38/38 x3; frame rate at 1255 MHz unchanged (Arkham 25.35 vs 25.15 fps, Hades 227.7 vs 228.5); no shareability faults in 8 Hades runs
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c        | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h          |  6 ++++++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
index a2b9f949..ff3f4eb3 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -499,7 +499,8 @@ kbase_dev_query_props(struct kbase_kmod_dev *kbase_dev,
                                 PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_MMAP |
                                 PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_WB_MMAP |
                                 PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_GPU_UNCACHED |
-                                PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_CSF_EVENT;
+                                PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_CSF_EVENT |
+                                PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT;
 }
 
 /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -1891,6 +1892,18 @@ kbase_kmod_import_dmabuf(struct pan_kmod_dev *dev,
       BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_RD | BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_WR |
       BASE_MEM_IMPORT_SHARED | BASE_MEM_COHERENT_LOCAL;
 
+   /* Our own dma-heap buffers that are never exported (the dma-buf only backs
+    * placed CPU maps) are written by the CPU through a cached mapping and read
+    * by no other driver. Map them outer-shareable so the GPU snoops the CPU
+    * caches (ACE-Lite); inner-shareable, the GPU can read memory the CPU's
+    * writes haven't reached yet (Arkham Asylum: staging lines read as zeros,
+    * which ASTC decodes to magenta). PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL=1 keeps them
+    * inner-shareable. */
+   if (!external_import && (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT) &&
+       !debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_KBASE_PRIVATE_LOCAL", false))
+      import_flags = (import_flags & ~BASE_MEM_COHERENT_LOCAL) |
+                     BASE_MEM_COHERENT_SYSTEM;
+
    if (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_GPU_UNCACHED)
       import_flags |= BASE_MEM_UNCACHED_GPU;
    if (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_WB_MMAP)
diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h
index 410c410d..1d71715b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h
@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ enum pan_kmod_bo_flags {
 
    /* kbase CSF event memory monitored for cross-CSG synchronization. */
    PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_CSF_EVENT = BITFIELD_BIT(8),
+
+   /* The buffer object is never exported to another process or driver. Some
+    * backends still give it a shareable backing (kbase backs placed CPU maps
+    * with a dma-buf); this tells them nobody else will map it.
+    */
+   PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT = BITFIELD_BIT(9),
 };
 
 /* Allowed group priority flags. */
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
index 37d7d6e5..cb5dd114 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
@@ -132,6 +132,12 @@ panvk_AllocateMemory(VkDevice _device,
          (device->vk.enabled_features.memoryMapPlaced &&
           (type->propertyFlags & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT));
 
+      /* Shareable only for placed maps: nobody else will map it. */
+      if (shareable && !can_be_exported &&
+          (device->kmod.dev->props.supported_bo_flags &
+           PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT))
+         bo_flags |= PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_EXPORT;
+
       bo_flags = panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags(device, bo_flags);
       mem->bo = pan_kmod_bo_alloc(device->kmod.dev,
                                   shareable ? NULL : device->kmod.vm,
